[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (8,4.6);
\node[anchor=north west, font=\small] at (0.15,4.5) {$\xi$};
\draw (3,2.3) circle (1.7);
\draw (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\node at (1.9,4.15) {$A$};
\node at (6.1,4.15) {$B$};
\node at (2.15,2.3) {$2$};
\node at (4,2.3) {$1$};
\node at (5.85,2.3) {$1$};
\node at (7.3,0.5) {$2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The Venn diagram shows the $6$ outcomes of rolling a standard six-sided die, where $A$ is 'the number is odd' and $B$ is 'the number is a multiple of $3$'. Are $A$ and $B$ mutually exclusive?
